  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their `default_map` entries; the full suite passes (1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n**Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`), a child context inherited the parent's whole `default_map` instead of the entry for its own command name. A map like `{\"foo\": {\"name\": \"mapped\"}}` was therefore searched for `name` at the top level and never found.\n\n**Fix:** the child now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, so the `foo` command gets `{\"name\": \"mapped\"}`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_default_map_subcommand` in `tests/test_defaults.py`. I didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry or touch `docs/`, which CLAUDE.md asks for on user-visible changes; say if you want those.",
